= January 1950

[? if dues_received_this_month > 0: Annual subscriptions have brought
[+ dues_received_this_month +] resources into the common treasury. ?]

[? if election_project_stage > 0 and election_project = "Constituency report archive":
Earlier work comparing constituency reports has left the
{!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} with specific
contacts and records; it has not removed administrative pressure from the
rerun. ?]
[? if election_project_stage > 0 and election_project = "Constituency test cases":
Earlier constitutional petitions have given the
{!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} several prepared
cases; they have not removed administrative pressure from the rerun. ?]
[? if election_project_stage > 0 and election_project = "Public election register":
Earlier publication of a provisional constituency register has exposed
specific gaps and disputed reports; it has not removed administrative
pressure from the rerun. ?]
[? if crown_pressure >= 65: Royal and administrative pressure is severe
enough that a general campaign will not protect every contest equally. ?]

The disputed Tehran election is cancelled and must be rerun. Cancellation does
not hand the {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}National
Front{!</span>!} a victory. It creates another contest in which royal and
administrative influence remain powerful and the opposition's people, money,
and documentary capacity remain limited.

The {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} must decide where to concentrate. A common slate can prevent allied
candidates from dividing their support. Monitoring can preserve cases for
later credential disputes. Attempting both requires additional resources and
will be less concentrated in either direction.

- @rerun_slate
- @rerun_monitor
- @rerun_balanced

@rerun_slate
title: Concentrate on a common Tehran slate
subtitle: A recognizable Tehran list concentrates the campaign and leaves fewer hands to document interference elsewhere
on-arrival: election_strategy = "Concentrated Tehran slate"; independent_nationalists_organization += 4; iran_party_relation += 2; public_mandate += 2

The coalition negotiates a limited common slate and directs its organizers
toward those candidacies. {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Independent nationalists{!</span>!} gain access to party
workers they could not command alone, while the {!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Iran Party{!</span>!} sees a clearer
connection between its effort and the agreed campaign.

Fewer people remain available to document every disputed polling place. The
{!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} enters the credential phase with a more coherent political group and a
less comprehensive evidentiary record.

- @post_event: Continue

@rerun_monitor
title: Build a common election-monitoring record
subtitle: The <span class="term term-national-front">Front</span> prepares cases that can survive scrutiny, even if its candidates receive less concentrated help
on-arrival: election_strategy = "Monitoring and credential record"; parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 5; organizational_reach += 3

Lawyers, editors, and local contacts use a common form for reports about
returns and interference. They distinguish a witness, a copied document, and
an allegation that still needs corroboration.

The network will be useful when credentials reach the {!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!}. It does not
solve the coalition's candidate coordination, and some local workers resent
being assigned to record keeping rather than turnout.

- @post_event: Continue

@rerun_balanced
title: Fund a smaller slate and selective monitoring teams
subtitle: Two resources sustain both a modest slate and selected observers; neither effort dominates
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} needs 2 resources to sustain both operations.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; election_strategy = "Slate with selective monitoring"; independent_nationalists_organization += 2; parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 3; organizational_reach += 2

The {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} narrows both ambitions. It supports fewer candidacies through shared
machinery and sends trained monitors only where reports indicate the greatest
risk. Paying travel, printing, and coordination costs consumes funds that
could have supported later organizing.

Neither operation is as deep as a single-purpose campaign, but the coalition
carries a usable slate and a selective evidence file into the next phase.

- @post_event: Continue

