@razmara_assassination
title: <span class="term term-independent">Razmara</span> is assassinated
subtitle: A documented assailant does not resolve wider responsibility
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1951 and month >= 3 and razmara_assassination_seen = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 10
on-arrival: razmara_assassination_seen = 1

= 7 March 1951

{!<span class="term term-islamist">!}Khalil Tahmasabi{!</span>!}, a member of
{!<span class="term term-islamist">!}Fada'iyan-e Islam{!</span>!},
assassinates {!<span class="term term-independent">!}Prime Minister Haj Ali
Razmara{!</span>!}. The identity of the assailant does not settle who else
encouraged, knew of, or bears political responsibility for the killing.

The {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} has opposed {!<span class="term term-independent">!}Razmara{!</span>!} on oil. That political conflict is not evidence
that the coalition authorized his murder. Its statement must respond to the
killing while religious-political allies, the {!<span class="term term-royalist">!}Court{!</span>!}, newspapers, and deputies
watch for different signals.

[? if hazhir_response = "Unqualified condemnation": The coalition's earlier
unqualified response to Hazhir's assassination creates pressure to use the
same standard now. ?]
[? if hazhir_response = "Joint constitutional statement": The earlier joint
statement offers a precedent for separating condemnation from unsupported
claims of responsibility. ?]
[? if hazhir_response = "Delayed verified statement": The delay after
Hazhir's assassination is remembered by editors who do not want another
silence in a political crisis. ?]

Nationalization remains before the institutions. How should the {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} keep
its oil case separate from an act of political violence?

- @assassination_condemn
- @assassination_bounded
- @assassination_verify

@assassination_condemn
title: Condemn the killing without qualification
subtitle: The <span class="term term-national-front">Front</span> refuses to let an opponent's murder stand in for a parliamentary victory, risking a breach with allies who read the killing differently
on-arrival: assassination_response = "Unqualified condemnation"; constitutional_legitimacy += 5; religious_network_relation -= 2; shah_relation += 1

The {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} issues an immediate condemnation and refuses to treat the death of a
political opponent as a substitute for parliamentary victory. The statement
assigns no collective responsibility beyond the documented assailant.

The {!<span class="term term-royalist">!}Court{!</span>!} receives an unambiguous constitutional signal. Some
religious-political partners think the {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} has separated the killing from
the oil conflict so sharply that it has ignored the confrontation surrounding
it.

- @post_event: Continue

@assassination_bounded
title: Condemn the killing and restate the constitutional oil case
subtitle: The statement condemns the murder and insists the oil case proceed on its own constitutional record
on-arrival: assassination_response = "Bounded constitutional statement"; constitutional_legitimacy += 3; parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 2; oil_coalition_support += 2

The statement condemns the assassination, denies that violence can decide the
oil question, and asks the committee and {!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!} to proceed through their own
record. It makes no allegation about prior knowledge or encouragement.

Coalition partners can continue the nationalization campaign without treating
{!<span class="term term-independent">!}Razmara{!</span>!}'s death as its mandate. The carefully bounded language satisfies
neither those demanding only condemnation nor those demanding only
mobilization.

- @post_event: Continue

@assassination_verify
title: Limit comment while wider responsibility is investigated
subtitle: The <span class="term term-national-front">Front</span> says only what it can prove, leaving an immediate silence others will fill
on-arrival: assassination_response = "Limited verified comment"; parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 2; constitutional_legitimacy -= 2; press_capacity -= 1; shah_relation -= 2

The {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} condemns the act itself but postpones a fuller statement while
lawyers and political contacts seek verified information about the
circumstances. They explicitly refuse to turn unanswered questions into
insinuation.

The caution protects the coalition's evidentiary standard. In the immediate
crisis, it also creates an ambiguous silence that newspapers and the {!<span class="term term-royalist">!}Court{!</span>!}
fill with their own interpretations.

- @post_event: Continue

