= 8 March 1951 — the committee

The oil committee recommends that the oil industry throughout Iran be
nationalized. The recommendation answers the policy question that followed
rejection of Gass–Golshayan. It is not yet an act of the full {!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!}.

The principle does not settle operational control, marketing, personnel
authority, compensation, interim finance, or the machinery of implementation.

[? if assassination_response = "Unqualified condemnation": The coalition
reaches the committee having denied itself any claim that violence supplied a
mandate for the vote. ?]
[? if assassination_response = "Bounded constitutional statement": Its
statement preserved the oil case while explicitly separating it from the
killing. ?]
[? if assassination_response = "Limited verified comment": Its caution
protected the evidentiary boundary but weakened the common public voice at the
moment of decision. ?]

- @majles_vote_resolution: Follow the report to the <span class="term term-parliament">Majles</span>

