- @nationalization_public
- @nationalization_cross_chamber

@majles_nationalization_defeat
title: The <span class="term term-parliament">Majles</span> rejects the principle
new-page: true

= 15 March 1951 — the {!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!}

Of [+ majles_attending_members +] members able to sit and attend, [+
nationalization_majles_support +] support the principle, [+
nationalization_majles_conditional +] withhold a firm commitment, and [+
nationalization_majles_opposed +] oppose it. The required majority is [+
nationalization_majles_threshold +].

The committee recommendation reaches the floor, but the opposition has not
converted its public case and parliamentary contacts into that majority.

This is a counterfactual result. The documented historical chamber approved
the principle; this campaign ends because the political state created by the
player does not reproduce that majority.

- @campaign_ending: Evaluate the campaign

@nationalization_institution
